{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a photodivergent strategy for the hydro- and oxoalkylation of vinyl arenes using 1,3-dicarbonyls. By switching between a Cu(II) photocatalyst under aerobic conditions and a 4CzIPN/Br\u00f8nsted base system under nitrogen, the authors can selectively produce oxoalkylated or hydroalkylated products. These two pathways are further combined synergistically in a formal [4+1]-annulation to synthesize stereoselective cyclopentanol derivatives.",
